options:
	-h: show this help screen
	-p [passkey]: passkey. Set to file:[filename] to read from file. Set to IP:[filename] to read from IP.
	-f [filename]: file to operate on
	-m [E/D]: set mode. (E)ncrypt or (D)ecrypt. Encrypt by default. 
	-i [IP:PORT]: IP and port to read from. 127.0.0.1:8000 by default
	-o [filename]: output file name

example usage:
	./encrypt.sh -m E -p file:keys.txt -o enc.txt -f secret.txt
	./encrypt.sh -m E -p IP:keys.txt -i: 127.0.0.1:8000 -o enc.txt -f secret.txt
